\label{lem:weighted-moment-stabilizer} Let $w_1,\ldots,w_M\in\mathbb C^*$ and let $V\subseteq\mathbb C^M$ be a linear space on which \[ \sum_{
u=1}^M w_
u v_
u =\sum_{
u=1}^M w_
u v_
u^2 =\sum_{
u=1}^M w_
u v_
u^3=0. \] Products of vectors are coordinatewise, and products of subspaces denote their linear spans. Put \[ U=\mathbb C\mathbf1+V,\qquad W=U^2,\qquad H=\operatorname{St}(W). \] If $H\cap V=0$, then \[ 3\dim V+\dim H\le M. \] In particular $3\dim V\le M-1$.
